<p>On the basis of exchange rates from 26 May - 04 June, the UK average RMG is above +5 per cent at 5.629 per cent. Since today is the last day of published rates for the period, the UK green rate will revalue to 1 ecc=GBP 0.720829 on Thursday, June 5, having successfully completed five confirmation periods. Since the halving of the UK RMG to 2.815 per cent creates a negative threshold of -2.185(=2.815.5), no devaluations are currently forecast for June 5. The ending of the confirmation process will signal the return of the 3-day (6 per cent) rule and, in addition, there will be a shortened reference period running from 5 - 10 June prior to the return to normal reference periods.</p>
